{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "כי ישבו אחים יחדו", :translit "ki yeshvu achim yachdav", :gloss "when brethren dwell together"} {:he "לא תחסום", :translit "lo tachsom", :gloss "you shall not muzzle"} {:he "יבמה שנפלה לפני מוכה שחין", :translit "yevamah she-naphlah lifnei mukah shechin", :gloss "a yevamah who falls before one afflicted with boils"} {:he "אין חוסמין אותה", :translit "ein chosmin otah", :gloss "they do not muzzle her"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Juxtaposition (semikhut) of adjacent parashiyot: the prohibition of muzzling (Deut 25:4) is placed immediately before the passage about yibbum to derive that a yevamah is not restrained from yibbum."}], :frame {:text "The principle of semikhut parashiyot — deriving law from the placement of adjacent passages — is a recognized hermeneutical method (Sifrei Zuta 25:4; Rashi on Deut 25:4 citing Sifrei). The application here concerns whether a yevamah who falls to a levir afflicted with boils (mukah shechin) may refuse yibbum or perform chalitzah.", :sources ["Sifrei Zuta 25:4" "Rashi on Deuteronomy 25:4"]}} {:quotes [{:he "ובן אין לו", :translit "u-ven ein lo", :gloss "and a son he does not have"} {:he "ס\"ת אונן עם אל\"ף", :translit "sat onan im alef", :gloss "end-letters spell onan with alef"} {:he "אונן", :translit "onan", :gloss "one mourning before burial"} {:he "דש מבפנים וזורה מבחוץ", :translit "dosh mibifnim u-zoreh mibachutz", :gloss "threshing indoors and winnowing outdoors"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :sofei-tevot, :phrase "ובן אין לו", :spells "אונן"} {:kind :other, :note "The alef in the phrase provides the alef in אונן; combined with the three final letters it spells the word."}], :frame {:text "The word onan (אונן) normally denotes a mourner before burial (Moed Katan 15a). The phrase 'who would thresh indoors and winnow outdoors' alludes to the biblical figure Onan son of Judah, who practiced coitus interruptus to avoid fulfilling levirate duty, described as 'destroying his seed to the ground' (Genesis 38:9–10), an act the rabbis likened to threshing without completing the process.", :sources ["Genesis 38:9–10" "Moed Katan 15a"]}} {:quotes [{:he "לאשה ויבמה", :translit "la-isha ve-yevamah", :gloss "for a wife and a yevamah"} {:he "ויבמה בעל כרחה", :translit "ve-yevamah ba-al karchah", :gloss "and a yevamah by force / against her will"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "ויבמה", :b "בעל כרחה"}], :frame nil}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Juxtaposition (semikhut) of adjacent parashiyot: the prohibition of muzzling (Deut 25:4) is placed immediately before the passage about yibbum to derive that a yevamah is not restrained from yibbum.", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :sofei-tevot, :phrase "ובן אין לו", :spells "אונן", :letters ["ן" "ן" "ו"], :by :selah, :order :mismatch} {:kind :other, :note "The alef in the phrase provides the alef in אונן; combined with the three final letters it spells the word.", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :gematria, :a "ויבמה", :a-value 63, :b "בעל כרחה", :b-value 335, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:39:18.750487669Z", :model "glm-5.2"}